<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/inventions?focus=copper-smelting">Inventions &amp; Discoveries</a> · Tools and materials</p><h1 class="enc-title">Copper smelting</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 5000 BCE</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/copper">Copper</a> smelting is the production of copper from its ores at high temperature; the world's oldest securely dated evidence for it, from c. 5000 BCE, was found at Belovode on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rudnik">Rudnik</a> mountain in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serbia">Serbia</a>. The Chalcolithic, or Copper Age, between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/neolithic">Neolithic</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bronze-age">Bronze Age</a>, was characterised by the increasing use of smelted copper, although <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stone-tools">stone tools</a> still predominated. Andean civilisations appear to have invented copper smelting independently, and it developed independently in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/air-mountains">Aïr Mountains</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/niger-river">Niger</a> between 3000 and 2500 BCE.</p></div>
<section class="inv-entry"><h2 class="enc-section-title">On the inventions tree</h2><dl class="inv-entry-facts"><div><dt>First known</dt><dd>c. 5000 BCE</dd></div><div><dt>Where</dt><dd>Belovode, Serbia</dd></div></dl><p class="inv-entry-note"><span class="inv-k">Also arose independently</span>the Andes; the Aïr Mountains, Niger (3000–2500 BCE)</p><p class="inv-entry-note"><span class="inv-k">Note</span>A copper axe from Prokuplje in Serbia may be older, c. 5500 BCE, and smelting may have begun separately in Asia and in Europe.</p><div class="inv-entry-rel"><span class="inv-k">Built on</span><a class="inv-chip" href="/encyclopedia/control-of-fire">Control of fire<span>c. 1 million years ago</span></a></div><div class="inv-entry-rel"><span class="inv-k">Led to</span><a class="inv-chip" href="/encyclopedia/bronze">Bronze<span>c. 4650 BCE</span></a><a class="inv-chip" href="/encyclopedia/pyramid-of-djoser">The first stone pyramid<span>27th century BCE</span></a><a class="inv-chip" href="/encyclopedia/iron-smelting">Iron smelting<span>c. 2500 BCE</span></a><a class="inv-chip" href="/encyclopedia/coinage">Coinage<span>late 7th century BCE</span></a></div><p class="enc-article-foot"><a class="enc-random-link" href="/inventions?focus=copper-smelting">See it on the inventions tree &rarr;</a></p></section>
